21:The inclusion criteria of T1-weighted images
23:1) Healthy or healthy controls in each dataset.
25:2) Subjects aged between 0.3 and 13 years.
27:3) For subjects with multiple longitudinal T1-weighted images, only the image of the highest quality was included.
29:4) For every half-year interval, a maximum of 100 subjects/images were included.
37:The UNC/UMN Baby Connectome Project (BCP) is a lifespan connectome initiative supported by the National Institutes of Health (NIH). Its primary objective is to document the neurodevelopmental and behavioral features of typically developing infants in the first five years after birth. The data are collected at two sites: UNC and UMN. 3
45:This dataset was part of the Children School Functions and Brain Development Project (Beijing Cohort), which is a collaborative effort between the State Key Laboratory of Cognitive Neuroscience and Learning, Peking University, and Beijing Huirongguan Hospital. MRI data were acquired using a 3 T SIEMENS Prisma scanner in the Center for Magnetic Resonance Imaging Research at Peking University. 5
49:The ongoing Chinese Color Nest Project (CCNP) aims to create normative charts for brain structure and function across the human lifespan. It consists of three phases: developing CCNP (devCCNP), maturing CCNP (matCCNP) and aging CCNP (ageCCNP). Only the devCCNP dataset from 2013 to 2017 was used, which was acquired at Southwest University in Chongqing, China. 6
53:The Healthy Brain Network (HBN) aims to develop a shared biobank by compiling data from 10,000 participants in the New York region, with the initiative being orchestrated by the Child Mind Institute.7
57:The Human Connectome Project Development (HCPD) studies aim to expand the coverage of HCP to include a more comprehensive range of ages across the lifespan.8
61:The Infant Brain Imaging Study (IBIS) aims to identify the early emergence of network functional impairments prior to symptom consolidation. This long-term, multisite study is funded by the National Institutes of Health Autism Centers of Excellence program. Scans were performed while infants were naturally sleeping. 9
65:The multicenter database on perinatal factors in child brain-mind development (PeriCBD) aims to construct a brain-mind model that describes children with adverse perinatal factors in the age group with a high incidence of neurodevelopmental disorders (NDDs) in the State Key Laboratory of Cognitive Neuroscience and Learning at Beijing Normal University. PeriCBD has conducted trial-data collection at two central district hospitals, the Anyang Maternal and Child Health Hospital of Henan Province and the People's Hospital of Liangping District, Chongqing.10
69:The PING data resource aims to create a comprehensive database for standardized measurement of behavior and image phenotypes, supported by whole-genome genotyping obtained from typically developing children spanning a wide age range.11
73:The OpenNeuro dataset titled Pixar was acquired using a 3 Tesla Siemens Tim Trio scanner located at the Athinoula A. Martinos Imaging Center at Massachusetts Institute of Technology. Participants were instructed to stay quiet and watch Disney Pixar’s “Partly Cloudy” during the scan. 12
